{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"a3e0ddf3be9b8a10","type":"text","text":"## How Economies Benefit from the Existence of the Investment Industry\n\n\n\n\n\n","x":-460,"y":-400,"width":420,"height":120},
		{"id":"938b0bf13e13f050","type":"text","text":"## Economic Systems\n\nEconomic systems strive to efficiently allocate scarce resources to their most productive uses.\n\n**Capitalism**: Relies on private ownership and free markets to allocate resources.\n\n**Government Roles**: Vary from minimal intervention in capitalist markets to significant involvement in resource dependent, transition or planned economies.","x":-1280,"y":-680,"width":680,"height":240},
		{"id":"850787914f10c8eb","type":"text","text":"## Economic Benefits of the Investment Industry\n\n#### Efficient Resource Allocation\n\n* Channel **funds** from **savers** to **spenders**.\n* Eliminates the high time and capital costs of searching for investment opportunities, directing resources towards productive growth.\n\n#### Data Collection and Asset Valuation\n\n* Collects and processes macroeconomic, industry and corporate data.\n* Helps determine the **fundamental value** of real and financial assets, enabling accurate asset pricing. [[Market Inefficiencies.canvas]]\n\n#### Packaging Investment Services\n\n* Packages opportunities into structured products and pooled investment vehicles.\n* Reduces investment costs and expands market access for individual and institutional savers.\n\n#### Providing liquidity and lowering Transaction Costs\n\n* Liquidity: the ability to buy or sell assets quickly without causing a significant impact on prices.\n* Transaction costs: Costs incurred when trading securities \n\n","x":120,"y":-1000,"width":800,"height":660},
		{"id":"97aba432fd17bba2","type":"text","text":"## Impact on Long-Term Economic Growth\n\n* **Capital Formation**: Fostering productive capital deployment increases total economic output, raises company profitability and expands economic growth.\n* **Lower Costs of Capital**: Efficient markets lower borrowing and financing costs for companies and governments, encouraging ongoing capital supply.","x":-40,"y":-80,"width":640,"height":280}
	],
